[{"answer":"We're pleased to welcome Dr Martin Merrywhether of the Antarctic Centre in Christchurch, New Zealand","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/1.mp3"},{"answer":"who has come along to talk to us today about the role of the Centre and the Antarctic Treaty.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/2.mp3"},{"answer":"Now my first question is about the choice of location for the centre.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Why Christchurch? Was it because of the climate?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, actually, New Zealand is the second closest country to Antarctica","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/5.mp3"},{"answer":"and Christchurch is often used on Antarctic expeditions.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/6.mp3"},{"answer":"Right, so it's because of where we are... coupled with our historical role.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/7.mp3"},{"answer":"So tell us - what is the main purpose of the centre?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Oh well... we have two complementary roles.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/9.mp3"},{"answer":"One is as a scientific base for expeditions and research","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/10.mp3"},{"answer":"and the other is as an information centre.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/11.mp3"},{"answer":"Tell us something about the role as a scientific base.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/12.mp3"},{"answer":"We're able to provide information about what scientists should take with them to the South Pole -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/13.mp3"},{"answer":"for example, the centre contains a clothing warehouse","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/14.mp3"},{"answer":"where expeditions are supplied with suitable clothing for the extreme conditions.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/15.mp3"},{"answer":"I suppose you need a bit more than your normal winter coat!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/16.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, exactly","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/17.mp3"},{"answer":"and then there's also the specialist library and mapping services.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/18.mp3"},{"answer":"Right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/19.mp3"},{"answer":"And which countries are actually located at the centre?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/20.mp3"},{"answer":"Well... the centre houses research programmes for New Zealand,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/21.mp3"},{"answer":"for The United States as well as for Italy...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/22.mp3"},{"answer":"there's even a US post office at the American airforce base here.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/23.mp3"},{"answer":"Really?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/24.mp3"},{"answer":"And what does the visitor's centre offer?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/25.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, since very few people will ever experience the Antarctic first hand,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/26.mp3"},{"answer":"the visitors' centre aims to recreate the atmosphere of Antarctica.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/27.mp3"},{"answer":"There's a mock camp site where you can see inside an Antarctic tent and imagine yourself sleeping there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/28.mp3"},{"answer":"And the centre also acts as a showcase for the unique international co-operation","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/29.mp3"},{"answer":"which exists in Antarctica today.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/30.mp3"},{"answer":"What is it actually like at the South Pole?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/31.mp3"},{"answer":"I know you've been there on a number of occasions.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/32.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, I have and each time I'm struck by the awesome beauty of the place.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/33.mp3"},{"answer":"It's magnificent","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/34.mp3"},{"answer":"but you can really only visit it in the summer months.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/35.mp3"},{"answer":"October to March.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/36.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, because it's completely dark for four months of the year...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/37.mp3"},{"answer":"and, in addition, it has to be the coldest place on earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/38.mp3"},{"answer":"Colder than the North Pole?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/39.mp3"},{"answer":"Why's that?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/40.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, unlike the North Pole, which is actually a frozen sea,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Antarctica is a land mass shaped like a dome,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/42.mp3"},{"answer":"with the result that the winds blow down the slopes at speeds of up to 150 km an hour","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/43.mp3"},{"answer":"and that's what makes it so cold.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/44.mp3"},{"answer":"And one other interesting thing is that Antarctica is the driest continent on earth,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/45.mp3"},{"answer":"surprisingly, and so you have to drink large amounts of water when you're there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/46.mp3"},{"answer":"How old is Antarctica?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/47.mp3"},{"answer":"Oh, we're pretty sure it was part of a larger land mass but it broke away from the rest of the continent...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/48.mp3"},{"answer":"170 million years ago.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/49.mp3"},{"answer":"How can you be certain of this?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/50.mp3"},{"answer":"Because fossils and rocks have been discovered in Antarctica","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/51.mp3"},{"answer":"which are the same as those found in places such as Africa and Australia.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/52.mp3"},{"answer":"Amazing... to think that it was once attached to Africa...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/53.mp3"},{"answer":"Now let's just have a look at the Antarctic Treaty.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/54.mp3"},{"answer":"How far back does the idea of an international treaty go?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/55.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, as far back as the 19th century,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/56.mp3"},{"answer":"when 11 nations organised an international event.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/57.mp3"},{"answer":"When was that exactly?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/58.mp3"},{"answer":"In 1870.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/59.mp3"},{"answer":"And it was called the Polar Research Meeting.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/60.mp3"},{"answer":"And then, not long after that,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/61.mp3"},{"answer":"they organised something called the First International Polar Year.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/62.mp3"},{"answer":"And that took place when exactly?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/63.mp3"},{"answer":"Over two years from 1882 to 1883.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/64.mp3"},{"answer":"But it wasn't until the 1950s that the idea of an international treaty was proposed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/65.mp3"},{"answer":"And in 1959, the Treaty was actually signed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/66.mp3"},{"answer":"What do you see as the main achievements of the treaty?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/67.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, firstly, it means that the continent is reserved for peaceful use.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/68.mp3"},{"answer":"That's Article 1, isn't it?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/69.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/70.mp3"},{"answer":"That's important since the territory belongs to everyone.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/71.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes but not as important as Article 5,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/72.mp3"},{"answer":"which prohibits any nuclear explosions or waste disposal.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/73.mp3"},{"answer":"Which is marvellous.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/74.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, I'm afraid we're going to have to stop there because I'm afraid we've run out of time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/75.mp3"},{"answer":"Thanks for coming along today and telling us all about the centre and its work.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-7-test-2-part-3-2023-07-28-17-13-19/76.mp3"}]
